---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const updated = new Date(SITE.legalUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-CA', { year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric', timeZone: 'UTC' });
---

<Page
  title="Privacy | WorldTripMap"
  description="WorldTripMap has no accounts and does not upload your maps. This page explains what stays on your device, what a share link contains, and what we measure."
  h1="Privacy"
  lede="The short version: there are no accounts, your maps stay in your own browser, and we do not sell or share personal information."
  crumb="Privacy"
  path="/privacy/"
>
  <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}.</p>

  <h2>Your maps and posters</h2>
  <p>
    The places you mark, your bucket list, your poster settings and the display name you type are saved in your browser’s local storage
    on the device you are using. They are not sent to us and we cannot see them. Posters are drawn on your device, and the files you
    download are created there too.
  </p>
  <p>
    <em>Start over</em> on a map clears the places marked on that map. To remove everything this site has saved on this device,
    including poster settings and your display name, use the button below or clear this site’s data in your browser settings.
  </p>
  <div class="erase" id="erase" hidden>
    <p>
      <button class="btn btn--sm btn--quiet" type="button" id="erase-start">Delete everything saved on this device</button>
    </p>
    <div class="erase__confirm" id="erase-confirm" hidden>
      <p>This removes your maps, bucket lists, poster settings and display name from this browser. It cannot be undone.</p>
      <p class="erase__actions">
        <button class="btn btn--sm btn--danger" type="button" id="erase-yes">Delete it all</button>
        <button class="btn btn--sm btn--quiet" type="button" id="erase-no">Keep my maps</button>
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="erase__status" id="erase-status" role="status"></p>
  </div>
  <p>The items stored are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>wtm:v1:map:…</code>: the places marked on each map</li>
    <li><code>wtm:v1:places:…</code>: the places you ticked inside provinces and territories</li>
    <li><code>wtm:v1:poster:…</code>: your poster design choices for each map</li>
    <li><code>wtm:v1:profile</code>: the display name you last typed</li>
    <li>
      <code>wtm:v1:rollup-dismissed:…</code>: a note that you dismissed a suggestion, kept only until you close the tab
    </li>
    {SITE.analytics === 'ga4' && <li><code>wtm:v1:consent</code>: whether you allowed analytics</li>}
  </ul>

  <h2>Share and challenge links</h2>
  <p>
    When you choose <em>Share</em> or <em>Challenge a friend</em>, the places you marked as explored on that map (not the places ticked
    inside a province), and your display name if you added
    one, are written into the link itself, in the part after the “#”. Browsers do not send that part of a link to web servers, so it
    does not reach us.
  </p>
  <p>
    Anyone who has the link can see what is in it. Because no copy is kept on a server, there is nothing for us to delete or revoke: to
    stop sharing a map, stop passing the link on. Do not put anything in the display name that you would not want the people you send
    it to, or anyone they forward it to, to read.
  </p>

  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  {
    SITE.analytics === 'none' && (
      <p>This site does not use analytics, advertising trackers or cookies.</p>
    )
  }
  {
    SITE.analytics === 'plausible' && (
      <p>
        We use Plausible Analytics to count visits. It does not use cookies, does not store your IP address, and does not follow you to
        other sites. We see totals, such as how many times a page was opened and which country and type of device visits came from.
      </p>
    )
  }
  {
    SITE.analytics === 'ga4' && (
      <>
        <p>
          If you choose <em>Allow analytics</em>, we use Google Analytics 4 to count visits. It sets cookies and sends usage information
          to Google. If you choose <em>No thanks</em>, it is never loaded. You can change your mind at any time:
        </p>
        <p>
          <button class="btn btn--sm btn--quiet" type="button" id="reset-consent">
            Change my analytics choice
          </button>
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }
  {
    SITE.analytics !== 'none' && (
      <>
        <p>We also count these actions, so we know which parts of the site are used:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>the home page was opened, and a map was started or completed,</li>
          <li>a place was marked (the map and the running count, never which place),</li>
          <li>a poster was customized, or downloaded as PNG or PDF (the map, the design and the shape),</li>
          <li>a share was started, a challenge link was opened, or a comparison was viewed.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          These never include your display name, the places you marked, or the contents of a share link. Page addresses are recorded
          without the part after the “#”.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    Like every website, this one is delivered by a hosting company whose servers briefly record technical details of each request, such
    as IP address, time, the page requested and the browser used, to keep the service secure and working. We do not combine those
    records with anything else. Fonts and images are served from this site, so opening a page does not contact any other company
    {SITE.analytics === 'none' ? '.' : ' apart from the analytics service described above.'}
  </p>

  <h2>If you contact us</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us{SITE.contactEndpoint ? ' or use the contact form' : ''}, we use your address and message to reply and to fix what
    you reported. We do not add you to a mailing list.
    {SITE.contactEndpoint && ' The form is delivered to us by a form-handling service, which processes your message on our behalf.'}
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The site is suitable for general audiences and does not ask anyone for personal information. It is not directed at children under
    13, and we do not knowingly collect information from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    Because your maps are stored only on your device, you control them directly. For anything you have sent us by email, you can ask us
    to show you what we hold, correct it or delete it by writing to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If this page changes in a way that matters, we will update the date at the top and note what changed.</p>
</Page>

<script is:inline>
  // Lets a visitor wipe what this site saved in their browser, and only says "deleted" after checking that it is gone.
  (function () {
    var box = document.getElementById('erase');
    var start = document.getElementById('erase-start');
    var confirmBox = document.getElementById('erase-confirm');
    var yes = document.getElementById('erase-yes');
    var no = document.getElementById('erase-no');
    var status = document.getElementById('erase-status');
    if (!box || !start || !confirmBox || !yes || !no || !status) return;
    box.hidden = false;
    var PREFIX = 'wtm:v1:';
    var KEEP = 'wtm:v1:consent';

    function ours(store) {
      var keys = [];
      for (var i = 0; i < store.length; i++) {
        var key = store.key(i) || '';
        if (key.indexOf(PREFIX) === 0 && key !== KEEP) keys.push(key);
      }
      return keys;
    }
    function reset() {
      confirmBox.hidden = true;
      start.hidden = false;
    }

    start.addEventListener('click', function () {
      status.textContent = '';
      start.hidden = true;
      confirmBox.hidden = false;
      no.focus();
    });
    no.addEventListener('click', function () {
      reset();
      start.focus();
    });
    yes.addEventListener('click', function () {
      var left = -1;
      try {
        [window.localStorage, window.sessionStorage].forEach(function (store) {
          ours(store).forEach(function (key) { store.removeItem(key); });
        });
        left = ours(window.localStorage).length + ours(window.sessionStorage).length;
      } catch (e) {
        left = -1;
      }
      reset();
      status.textContent =
        left === 0
          ? 'Deleted. Nothing from your maps or posters is saved on this device now.'
          : 'Your browser did not let this page change its storage, so nothing was deleted. Clear this site’s data in your browser settings instead.';
      start.focus();
    });
  })();
</script>

{
  SITE.analytics === 'ga4' && (
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        var button = document.getElementById('reset-consent');
        if (!button) return;
        button.addEventListener('click', function () {
          try { localStorage.removeItem('wtm:v1:consent'); } catch (e) {}
          location.reload();
        });
      })();
    </script>
  )
}

<style>
  .erase {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
  .erase[hidden],
  .erase__confirm[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .erase__confirm {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.15rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-control);
    background: var(--white);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .erase__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .erase__status:empty {
    display: none;
  }
  .erase__status {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
